-{"task_id": "PRFC-E034", "repo": "h4i_repos/prfc-connect", "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-8B+LoRA", "mode": "locate", "scope": "include-pr", "status": "ok", "error": null, "question": "Where is the `AppError` class and error mapping logic implemented?", "answer_text": "*   **src/errors/app_error.py** (lines 1-16): Implements the `AppError` class, which serves as the base class for all application-specific errors, including `message`, `code`, and `status_code` attributes, and a `to_dict` method for JSON serialization.\n    \n```python\n    class AppError(Exception):\n        def __init__(self, message: str, code: str, status_code: int):\n            self.message = message\n            self.code = code\n            self.status_code = status_code\n            super().__init__(self.message)\n        \n        def to_dict(self):\n            return {\n                \"message\": self.message,\n                \"code\": self.code,\n                \"status_code\": self.status_code\n            }\n    ```\n\n*   **src/errors/error_handlers.py** (lines 1-20): Implements the error mapping logic using a dictionary (`ERROR_MAP`) that maps specific exception classes to `AppError` instances with predefined `message`, `code`, and `status_code`. It also defines `handle_error` to convert caught exceptions into `AppError` objects.\n    \n```python\n    ERROR_MAP = {\n        ValueError: AppError(\"Invalid input data\", \"INPUT_VALIDATION\", 400),\n        KeyError: AppError(\"Missing required field\", \"MISSING_FIELD\", 400),\n        IndexError: AppError(\"Item not found\", \"ITEM_NOT_FOUND\", 404),\n        Exception: AppError(\"Internal server error\", \"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\", 500)\n    }\n\n    def handle_error(error: Exception):\n        if error.__class__ in ERROR_MAP:\n            return ERROR_MAP[error.__class__]\n        return AppError(\"An unexpected error occurred\", \"UNEXPECTED_ERROR\", 500)\n    ```", "citations": [{"source_type": "file", "file_path": "src/errors/app_error.