     <TableCell align=\"center\">Actions</TableCell>\n                </TableRow>\n            </TableHead>\n            <TableBody>\n                {sortedReferrals.map((referral) => (\n                    <TableRow key={referral.id}>\n                        <TableCell>{referral.code}</TableCell>\n                        <TableCell>{referral.email}</TableCell>\n                        <TableCell align=\"center\">\n                            <Chip\n                                label={formatReferralStatus(referral.status)}\n                                color={statusColors[referral.status]}\n                            />\n                        </TableCell>\n                        <TableCell align=\"center\">{formatDateTime(referral.createdAt)}</TableCell>\n                        <TableCell align=\"center\">{referral.redeemedAt ? formatDateTime(referral.redeemedAt) : ''}</TableCell>\n                        <TableCell align=\"center\">\n                            {referral.status === 'pending' && (\n                                <IconButton\n                                    aria-label=\"Redeem\"\n                                    color=\"primary\"\n                                    onClick={() => handleRedeem(referral.id)}\n                                >\n                                    <CheckCircleOutlineIcon />\n                                </IconButton>\n                            )}\n                            {referral.status === 'redeemed' && (\n                                <IconButton\n                                    aria-label=\"Reissue\"\n                                    color=\"secondary\"\n                                    onClick={() => handleReissue(referral.id)}\n                                >\n                                    <ReplayIcon />\n                                </IconButton>\n                            )}\n                        </TableCell>\n                    </TableRow>\n                ))}\n            </TableBody>\n        </Table>\n        <TablePagination\n            rowsPerPageOptions={[10, 25, 50]}\n            component=\"div\"\n            count={referrals.length}\n            rowsPerPage={rowsPerPage}\n            page={page}\n            onPageChange={handleChangePage}\n            onRowsPerPageChange={handleChangeRowsPerPage}\n        />\n        ```\n\n        -   **Explanation**: The `sortedReferrals` array is derived from the `referrals` prop and `sortConfig` using `sortTableData`. The `TablePagination` component handles the display of pagination controls, including `rowsPerPage`, `page`, `onPageChange`, and `onRowsPerPageChange`.\n\n### 2. **Referral Filters (`ReferralFilters.tsx`)**\n\nThis component manages the state for filtering the referrals based on status and search query.\n\n-   **Filter State**:\n    -   **Cited at**: `src/components/referrals/ReferralFilters.tsx:12-17`\n    -   **Code**:\n        \n```typescript\n        const [statusFilter, setStatusFilter] = useState<string | 'all'>('all');\n        const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState<string>('');\n        ```\n\n    -   **Explanation**: `statusFilter` can be 'all', 'pending', or 'redeemed', allowing users to view referrals based on their status. `searchQuery` holds the text input for searching referral codes or emails.\n\n-   **Filter Application**:\n    -   **Cited at**: `src/components/referrals/ReferralFilters.tsx:39-41`\n    -   **Code**:\n        \n```typescript\n        const filteredReferrals = referrals.filter(referral =>\n            (statusFilter === 'all' || referral.status === statusFilter) &&\n            (referral.code.includes(searchQuery) || referral.email.includes(searchQuery))\n        );\n        ```\n\n    -   **Explanation**: The `filteredReferrals` array is created by applying both the `statusFilter` and `searchQuery` to the `referrals` array. This array is then passed to `ReferralListTable` to display only the relevant referrals.\n\n### 3. **Referral Drawer (`ReferralDrawer.tsx`)**\n\nThis component displays detailed information about a single referral and allows updating its status (e.g., redeeming or reissuing).\n\n-   **Selected Referral State**:\n    -   **Cited at**: `src/components/referrals/ReferralDrawer.tsx:15-17`\n    -   **Code**:\n        \n```typescript\n        const [selectedReferral, setSelectedReferral] = useState<Referral | null>(null);\n        const [isDrawerOpen, setIsDrawerOpen] = useState(false);\n        ```\n\n    -   **Explanation**: `selectedReferral` holds the data for the currently opened referral, and `isDrawerOpen` controls the visibility of the drawer.\n\n-   **Drawer Trigger**:\n    -   **Cited at**: `src/components/referrals/ReferralListTable.tsx:160-164`\n    -   **Code**:\n        \n```typescript\n            <TableCell align=\"center\">\n                {referral.status === 'pending' && (\n                    <IconButton\n                        aria-label=\"Redeem\"\n                        color=\"primary\"\n                        onClick={() => handleRedeem(referral.id)}\n                    >\n                        <CheckCircleOutlineIcon />\n                    </IconButton>\n                )}\n                {referral.status === 'redeemed' && (\n                    <IconButton\n                        aria-label=\"Reissue\"\n                        color=\"secondary\"\n                        onClick={() => handleReissue(referral.id)}\n                    >\n                        <ReplayIcon />\n                    </IconButton>\n                )}\n            </TableCell>\n        </TableRow>\n        <TablePagination\n            rowsPerPageOptions={[10, 25, 50]}\n            component=\"div\"\n            count={referrals.length}\n            rowsPerPage={rowsPerPage}\n            page={page}\n            onPageChange={handleChangePage}\n            onRowsPerPageChange={handleChangeRowsPerPage}\n        />\n        <Dialog\n            open